# Playwright conventions

Specs describe intent. Page objects own locators and actions. Follow `.cursor/skills/pom-conventions/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/skills/api-cleanup/SKILL.md`.

## Auth

Stored session by default. UI login only for login-page tests.

```ts
// Signed-in Didaxis spec
test.use({ storageState: authStorageFile });

// Login page only — empty session
test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } });
```

## Page objects

One class per page or component in `pages/`. Locators are `readonly` and set in the constructor. Methods perform actions. No `expect()` in a page object. Compose `NewProgramModal` on `ProgramsPage`.

## Locators

Use `getByRole` and `getByLabel`. `getByText` only for stable text the screen actually shows. No CSS, no XPath, and no locators in a spec.

```ts
// Spec
await programs.goto();
await programs.openNewProgramForm();
await expect(programs.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible();

// Not this
await page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' }).click();
```

## Data and cleanup

Name created records with `uniqueName()`, which appends `Date.now()`. Import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts`, not `@playwright/test`. Call `trackProgram(uuid)` as soon as a program is created. Do not write `afterAll` cleanup and do not delete through the UI.
